<p>The <strong>state</strong> is the smallest set of numbers that, with the future inputs, determines the future. For a mechanical system that is positions and velocities; for a circuit, capacitor voltages and inductor currents. Choosing physical states pays off later, when you design observers and Kalman filters that estimate them.</p>
